e county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 34 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 49% of normal in August to September and 56% in January to February. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 241% of normal on the middle. Every one of the 6 grids had its driest year in 1958, with grid 28681 lowest at 71% of normal.</p>"}
